  "title": "Bristol-Myers Squibb Co. (BMY): Admilparant Phase 3 IPF Trial Achieves Primary Endpoint, But Details Limited and Questions Remain",
  "type": "equity_research",
  "priority": "medium",
  "published": "2026-10-13",
  "insights": [
   "BMY's Phase 3 ALOFT-IPF trial for admilparant met the primary endpoint at the 60mg dose, showing statistically significant improvement in FVC vs placebo.",
   "The 120mg dose failed to show statistical significance in slowing FVC decline, challenging the dose-response thesis for the drug.",
   "Admilparant demonstrated a well-tolerated safety profile, with low discontinuation rates similar to placebo, helping to mitigate prior concerns regarding drug-induced liver injury.",
   "The admilparant IPF program represents a ~5% swing factor on the firm's BMY DCF, with current peak unadjusted sales modeled at $2.7bn for 2035.",
