   "Freight rates for tankers have surged 10-50x since the start of 2026, causing a wide divergence in realized margins for E&Ps and refiners globally.",
   "Shipping crude costs have risen up to $40/bbl on the longest hauls, with the average delivered cost across coverage increasing to $10.4/bbl from $1.0/bbl a year ago.",
   "North Sea and North American producers are relative winners due to end-market proximity, while Asian refiners face the greatest pressure from reliance on long-haul seaborne imports.",
